body.append('<h2>On the Field</h2>')
body.append(P('<b>Arkansas State men’s basketball</b> (3-2) opens three days of games in Miami this afternoon against Southern Utah at 2:30 p.m. at the Ocean Bank Convocation Center, in an event hosted by Florida International University. The Red Wolves play Long Beach State on Tuesday and FIU on Wednesday, also at 2:30, with all three on ESPN+. They come in off a 100-69 win over Arkansas-Pine Bluff and return to First National Bank Arena to play Rice on Sunday, Nov. 29, at 1 p.m.'))
body.append(P('<b>Arkansas State football</b> (4-7) closes its season Saturday against Troy at 2 p.m. at Centennial Bank Stadium, expected on ESPN+, in the second game under interim coach Jalen Ortiz. No permanent coach had been named as of Sunday; Hugh Freeze, who coached the Red Wolves in 2011, is still reported to be the leading candidate, but the school has not confirmed it.||<b>Red Wolves volleyball</b>, the Sun Belt’s outright regular-season champion, lost the conference tournament final to Georgia Southern 3-0 on Sunday in Foley, Ala., 25-16, 25-22, 25-23, after leading the third set 21-18. Addison Collum had 11 kills and four blocks, Erin Madigan 30 assists and Kaitlin Whitlock 22 digs. A-State is 21-9 and awaits word on the NCAA tournament field.'))
body.append(P('<b>Arkansas Razorbacks football</b> (4-7, 2-6 SEC) ends its season Saturday against LSU at 11:45 a.m. at Reynolds Razorback Stadium in Fayetteville, on the SEC Network. The Hogs are out of bowl contention after the 45-3 loss at Texas, the worst of first-year coach Ryan Silverfield’s tenure. LSU (6-5), under Lane Kiffin, has lost three straight. The teams play for the Golden Boot, which LSU has won four years running, 23-22 last season.'))
body.append(P('<b>Tennessee Vols football</b> rose two places to No. 7 in Sunday’s Associated Press poll after beating LSU and is 9-2 (6-2 SEC). The Vols close the regular season Saturday at Vanderbilt in Nashville at 6 p.m. Central on ESPN, the rivalry’s first night game since 2022; Vanderbilt is 4-7 but beat Tennessee in Knoxville last year. The College Football Playoff committee, which had the Vols ninth, releases its next ranking Tuesday night.'))

body.append('<h2>Afield &amp; Afloat</h2>')
body.append('<p class="note">Ratings are rule-of-thumb estimates from the forecast, the rut calendar and the sun, not measurements of animal or fish behavior.</p>')
body.append('<h3>Deer outlook: Excellent</h3>')
body.append(P('Everything lines up this morning: the rut is still in its peak window for north Arkansas, the dawn is cold, near 38 and some 18 degrees colder than Sunday’s, and the barometer is climbing steadily behind the front. The one drawback is the wind, about 12 miles an hour in the morning and 11 by evening. Best windows: from about 6:17 a.m. to roughly two hours after sunrise at 6:47, and from 2:50 p.m. until sunset at 4:50; in the rut, 10 a.m. to 2 p.m. is realistic for bucks cruising.||<i>Today’s tip:</i> the first cold, bright morning after a front is the one to take off work for, if you can. With modern gun closed in Zone 4, bowhunters should set up on the downwind edge of a doe bedding thicket, where a cruising buck will scent-check it, and stay put through midday; in Zones 3, 6 and 8 a rifle hunter on a long field edge can watch for a buck trailing does well after the sun is up.'))
body.append(P('<b>Tomorrow, Tuesday (estimate: Excellent).</b> An even colder dawn, near 31, with the barometer at its highest of the week and starting to ease under a thickening gray sky ahead of Wednesday’s damp weather; the wind about 13 miles an hour in the morning and 11 or 12 by evening. Windows: about 6:18 a.m. to two hours after sunrise at 6:48, and 2:50 p.m. to sunset at 4:50, with 10 a.m. to 2 p.m. still worth a sit.||<i>Tomorrow’s tip:</i> deer often feed hard ahead of a change in the weather, so the last two hours of daylight Tuesday may be the best evening of the week; hunt the food: a cut bean field, a winter wheat planting or a white-oak flat still dropping acorns. Frost on the ground makes every step loud, so get to the stand early and let the woods settle.'))
body.append('<h3>Fishing outlook: Fair</h3>')
body.append(P('The cold snap has only just arrived, and fish on Craighead Forest Lake and Lake Frierson tend to sulk for a day after a sharp drop like Sunday’s; the bright sun, an afternoon near 50 and a light chop from the breeze help some. Best times: late morning through mid-afternoon as the water warms, and the last hour before sunset at 4:50.||<i>Today’s tip:</i> look for the warmest water you can find: a north-bank pocket or a rocky shoreline that has had the sun on it since noon. A slowly worked jig or a small suspending jerkbait, paused for several seconds between twitches, suits cold-front bass, and crappie should be tight to brush in 12 to 18 feet of water.'))
body.append(P('<b>Tomorrow, Tuesday (estimate: Fair).</b> A cold, cloudy day near 45, with the barometer starting a slow fall ahead of Wednesday’s rain, which often wakes fish up for a feed. Best times: late morning through mid-afternoon, plus the last hour before sunset at 4:50.||<i>Tomorrow’s tip:</i> overcast skies let fish roam a little shallower; try a small crappie jig or minnow under a slip float over brush near the creek channel, and for catfish, cut shad or chicken liver fished on the bottom off the dam or a deep point.'))

body.append('<h3>In season now, and what is next (zones 3, 4, 6 and 8)</h3>')
body.append(ZONE)
body.append(P('<b>Deer.</b> Zone 4, which includes Craighead County, closed its modern gun season Sunday evening; Zone 4 hunters now have archery through Feb. 28 and the statewide Christmas holiday modern gun hunt, Dec. 26-28, and Zone 4 has no muzzleloader (Alternative Firearms) season. In Zones 3, 6 and 8, modern gun runs through Sunday, Dec. 6, followed by the Dec. 12-14 Alternative Firearms weekend and the same holiday hunt. The limit in every zone is four deer, no more than two antlered bucks; in Zone 4 only one antlerless deer may be taken by modern gun, while Zones 3, 6 and 8 allow three antlerless by gun and muzzleloader combined. The youth modern gun weekend returns Jan. 2-3.'))
body.append(P('<b>Ducks and geese.</b> The first duck segment is open through Sunday, Nov. 29, then closes until the second, Dec. 10-23, and the third, Dec. 26 through Jan. 31. The daily limit is six ducks, with no more than four mallards (two hens), three wood ducks, three pintails, two redheads, two canvasbacks, two black ducks, one mottled duck and one scaup; Canada geese two a day, white-fronted geese two, and snow, blue and Ross’s geese 20. On wildlife management areas, shooting ends at noon. Thanksgiving morning in the blind is an old Arkansas custom; mind the low water, and check the weekly water report on agfc.com before you go.||<b>Small game.</b> Quail season runs through Feb. 7 (six a day), rabbit through Feb. 28 (eight a day) and squirrel through Feb. 28 (12 a day, dogs allowed).'))

body.append('<h2>Postscript</h2>')
body.append('<p class="ps" style="margin-left:2em">Thou that hast giv’n so much to me,<br>Give one thing more, a gratefull heart.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;. . .<br>Not thankfull, when it pleaseth me;<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;As if thy blessings had spare dayes:<br>But such a heart, whose pulse may be<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thy praise.</p>')
body.append('<p class="ps">&mdash; George Herbert, “Gratefulnesse,” from <i>The Temple</i> (1633), first two lines and last stanza, in the poet’s spelling. At the start of Thanksgiving week, the old parson asks for thanks that keeps no holidays, a heart grateful on ordinary days too.</p>')
body.append('<p class="sign">Until tomorrow, with good wishes &mdash;<br><b>The Editor</b></p>')
body.append('<div class="foot">Compiled from many reports.</div>')

# Pastimes
import os, json as _json
fleet = _json.load(open('fleet.json')) if os.path.exists('fleet.json') else None
def fleet_svg(d):
    n=d['size']; cs=30; lab=18; W=lab+n*cs; H=lab+n*cs
    o=[f'<svg viewBox="0 0 {W} {H}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;font-family:inherit">']
    for c in range(n): o.append(f'<text x="{lab+c*cs+cs/2}" y="12" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#8a6a35">{chr(65+c)}</text>')
    for r in range(n):
        o.append(f'<text x="{lab/2}" y="{lab+r*cs+cs/2+4}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#4a3618">{r+1}</text>')
        for c in range(n):
            x=lab+c*cs;y=lab+r*cs
            o.append(f'<rect x="{x}" y="{y}" width="{cs}" height="{cs}" fill="none" stroke="#8a6a35" stroke-width="1"/><text x="{x+cs/2}" y="{y+cs/2+6}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="bold" fill="#2b2118">{d["grid"][r][c]}</text>')
    o.append('</svg>'); return ''.join(o)
body.append('<div class="page pastimes"><h2>The Pastimes</h2>')
left='<div><h3>I. Mate in Two</h3>'+f'<div class="board">{past["chess_svg"]}</div>'+f'<p>{past["chess_prompt"]} White is shown with the lighter, outlined pieces; the board is oriented with White at the bottom.</p></div>'
if fleet:
    tot=sum(len(x['word']) for x in fleet['ships'])
    clues=''.join(f'<li><span class="bl">{" ".join("_" for _ in x["word"])}</span> ({len(x["word"])}) {x["hint"]}</li>' for x in fleet['ships'])
    right=('<div><h3>II. Word Fleet</h3>'+'<div style="width:84%">'+fleet_svg(fleet)+'</div>'+
      f'<ol class="clues fl">{clues}</ol>'
      f'<p class="note">Each clue is a definition. Find its word in the grid, across or down. Fire by putting a pencil dot on a letter: one dot is one shot. Check the answers below, then circle each right letter and cross out each wrong one. Your score is your number of dots. <b>Best possible score: {tot} shots.</b> My shots: ________</p></div>')
    sol_ii='II. '+', '.join(f"{x['word']} {chr(65+x['c'])}{x['r']+1} {'across' if x['dir']=='A' else 'down'}" for x in fleet['ships'])
else:
    right='<div><h3>II. The Four Houses</h3>'+f'<p>{past["logic_intro"]}</p><ol class="clues">'+''.join(f'<li>{c}</li>' for c in past['logic_clues'])+f'</ol><p>{past["logic_question"]}</p></div>'
    sol_ii='II. '+past['logic_answer']
body.append('<div class="two">'+left+right+'</div>')
if os.path.exists('comic/today.svg'):
    body.append('<h3 style="margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0">III. Sorry, Earth</h3><div class="comic" style="margin:1pt 0 0 0"><img src="comic/today.png" style="width:92%;display:block;margin:0 auto"></div>')
body.append('<div class="flip box"><b>Solutions printed upside down.</b><br>I. '+past['chess_solution']+'<br>'+sol_ii+'</div></div>')

html = f'<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>The Morning Letter</title><style>{css}</style></head><body>'+'\n'.join(body)+'</body></html>'
open('letter.html','w').write(html)
print(len(html))

